      "[('what is mongo db', '1. MongoDB ─ Overview . 2 2. MongoDB ─ Advantages . 4'), ('what is mongo db', 'MongoDB 5 MongoDB is a cross-platform, document oriented database that provides, high performance, high availability, and easy scalability. MongoDB works on concept of collection and document. Database Database is a physical container for collections. Each database gets its own set of files on the file system. A single MongoDB server typically has multiple databases. Collection'), ('what is mongo db', '\\uf0b7 Big Data \\uf0b7 Content Management and Delivery \\uf0b7 Mobile and Social Infrastructure 2. MongoDB ─ Advantages'), ('what is mongo db', 'MongoDB i About the T utorial MongoDB is an open -source document database and leading NoSQL database. MongoDB is written in C++. This tutorial will give you great understanding on MongoDB concepts needed to create and deploy a highly scalable and performance-oriented database. Audience This tutorial is designed for Software Professionals who are willing to learn MongoDB'), ('what is mongo db', 'MongoDB 7 Any relational database has a typical schema design that shows number of tables and the relationship between these tables. While in MongoDB, there is no concept of relationship. Advantages of MongoDB over RDBMS \\uf0b7 Schema less: MongoDB is a document database in which one collection holds different documents. Number of fields, content and size of the document can differ from one'), ('what is mongo db', \"document to another. \\uf0b7 Structure of a single object is clear. \\uf0b7 No complex joins. \\uf0b7 Deep query -ability. MongoDB supports dynamic queries on documents using a document-based query language that's nearly as powerful as SQL. \\uf0b7 Tuning. \\uf0b7 Ease of scale-out: MongoDB is easy to scale. \\uf0b7 Conversion/mapping of application objects to database objects not needed.\"), ('what is mongo db', '7. MongoDB ─ Create Collection . 14 8. MongoDB ─ Drop Collection . 16'), ('what is mongo db', '11. MongoDB ─ Query Document . 20 12. MongoDB ─ Update Document . 24'), ('what is mongo db', 'MongoDB 12'), ('what is mongo db', 'Collection Collection is a group of MongoDB documents. It is the equivalent of an RDBMS table. A collection exists within a single database. Collections do not enforce a schema. Documents within a collection can have different fields. Typically, all documents in a collection are of similar or related purpose. Document'), ('what is mongo db', 'MongoDB 13 MongoDB Statistics To get stats about MongoDB server, type the command db.stats() in MongoDB client. This will show the database name, number of collection and documents in the database. Output of the command is shown in the following screenshot.'), ('what is mongo db', '9. MongoDB ─ Datatypes . 17 10. MongoDB ─ Insert Document . 18'), ('what is mongo db', 'MongoDB 4 MongoDB'), ('what is mongo db', 'MongoDB 14 Data in MongoDB has a flexible schema.documents in the same collection. They do not need to have the same set of fields or structure, and common fields in a collection’s documents may hold different types of data. Some considerations while designing Schema in MongoDB \\uf0b7 Design your schema according to user requirements.'), ('what is mongo db', 'MongoDB 20 In this chapter, we will see how to create a collection using MongoDB. The createCollection() Method MongoDB db.createCollection(name, options) is used to create collection. Syntax Basic syntax of createCollection() command is as follows: db.createCollection(name, options) In the command, name is name of collection to be created. Options is a document and is'), ('what is mongo db', '17. MongoDB ─ Indexing . 32 18. MongoDB ─ Aggregation . 34'), ('what is mongo db', \"MongoDB 6 mysql/sqlplus mongo Sample Document Following example shows the document structure of a blog site , which is simply a comma separated key value pair. { _id: ObjectId(7df78ad8902c) title: 'MongoDB Overview', description: 'MongoDB is no sql database', by: 'tutorials point', url: 'http://www.tutorialspoint.com', tags: ['mongodb', 'database', 'NoSQL'],\"), ('what is mongo db', '{ \"ok\" : 1 } > In MongoDB, you don\\'t need to create collection. MongoDB creates collection automatically, when you insert some document. >db.tutorialspoint.insert({\"name\" : \"tutorialspoint\"}) >show collections mycol mycollection system.indexes tutorialspoint >'), ('what is mongo db', '5. MongoDB ─ Create Database . 12 6. MongoDB ─ Drop Database . 13'), ('what is mongo db', '19. MongoDB ─ Replication . 38 20. MongoDB ─ Sharding. 41'), ('what is mongo db', '\\uf0b7 Uses internal memory for storing the (windowed) working set, enabling faster access of data. Why Use MongoDB? \\uf0b7 Document Oriented Storage: Data is stored in the form of JSON style documents. \\uf0b7 Index on any attribute \\uf0b7 Replication and high availability \\uf0b7 Auto-sharding \\uf0b7 Rich queries \\uf0b7 Fast in-place updates \\uf0b7 Professional support by MongoDB Where to Use MongoDB? \\uf0b7 Big Data'), ('what is mongo db', '24. MongoDB ─ PHP . 60 ADVANCED MONGODB . . . . 66'), ('what is mongo db', '31. MongoDB ─ Indexing Limitations . 80 32. MongoDB ─ ObjectId . 81'), ('what is mongo db', 'Database Database Table Collection Tuple/Row Document column Field Table Join Embedded Documents Primary Key Primary Key (Default key _id provided by mongodb itself) Database Server and Client Mysqld/Oracle mongod 1. MongoDB ─ Overview'), ('what is mongo db', 'MongoDB 16 So while showing the data, in RDBMS you need to join three tables and in MongoDB, data will be shown from one collection only.'), ('what is mongo db', 'Restart MongoDB sudo service mongodb restart To use MongoDB run the following command. mongo This will connect you to running MongoDB instance. MongoDB Help To get a list of commands , type db.help() in MongoDB client. This will give you a list of commands as shown in the following screenshot.'), ('what is mongo db', \"MongoDB 17 In this chapter, we will see how to create a database in MongoDB. The use Command MongoDB use DATABASE_NAME is used to create database. The command will create a new database if it doesn't exist, otherwise it will return the existing database. Syntax Basic syntax of use DATABASE statement is as follows: use DATABASE_NAME Example\"), ('what is mongo db', 'Your created database (mydb) is not present in list. To display database , you need to insert at least one document into it. >db.movie.insert({\"name\":\"tutorials point\"}) >show dbs local 0.78125GB mydb 0.23012GB 5. MongoDB ─ Create Database'), ('what is mongo db', '35. MongoDB ─ Regular Expression . 88 36. MongoDB ─ RockMongo . 90'), ('what is mongo db', 'MongoDB 11 Next install the MongoDB by using the following command − apt-get install mongodb-10gen=2.2.3 In the above installation , 2.2.3 is currently released MongoDB version. Make sure to install the latest version always. Now MongoDB is installed successfully. Start MongoDB sudo service mongodb start Stop MongoDB sudo service mongodb stop Restart MongoDB'), ('what is mongo db', \"MongoDB 18 test 0.23012GB In MongoDB default database is test. If you didn't create any database , then collections will be stored in test database.\"), ('what is mongo db', \"MongoDB 19 In this chapter, we will see how to drop a database using MongoDB command. The dropDatabase() Method MongoDB db.dropDatabase() command is used to drop a existing database. Syntax Basic syntax of dropDatabase() command is as follows: db.dropDatabase() This will delete the selected database. If you have not selected any database, then it will delete default 'test' database.\")]\n",
